WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.380
More than 10,000 jobs ride on TSMC's Arizona expansion ground-breaking December 4th. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, episode 66.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:25.520
Huawei's memory papers, a stop on servers into Southeast Asia, and a server power supply design come next. Then the gap between multi-year chip commitments and a grid that still has to connect. President Donald Trump is the headliner, and a TSMC spokesperson has confirmed he will be there.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:31.480
Cho Sun, citing Bloomberg and a White House official, says TSMC executives and people from

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.900
suppliers and customers are expected in the room.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.860
Whether Jensen Huang shows up is still open.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.560
The first Arizona plant is already running and Vidia Blackwell plus chips for AMD and Apple.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:47.260
12,000 to 15,000 construction and support workers are on the site now.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.680
TSMC first announced the plant near the end of Trump's first administration, then in

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:57.320
March last year put a $165 billion U.S. investment plan on the table.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.260
December 4th breaks ground on the expansion.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.500
It does not energize a new fab.

00:01:03.677 --> 00:01:08.457
Huawei and Chang's in-memory technologies are on the draft program IEEE released for

00:01:08.457 --> 00:01:12.537
the International Solid State Circuit's conference in San Francisco next February.

00:01:13.257 --> 00:01:14.017
Fen news reports.

00:01:14.877 --> 00:01:17.677
Huawei's slot is next-generation high-band with memory.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:23.557
US media said the data-pindensity is twice that of the Samsung and SK Heinix parts now

00:01:23.557 --> 00:01:28.217
in mass production, which in theory lifts bandwidth because the processor can pull more

00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:29.077
data per pin.

00:01:30.037 --> 00:01:35.257
CXMT's papers cover next-generation DDR5 and an LPDDR6 interface.

00:01:35.897 --> 00:01:41.457
Earlier this month, CXMT said it had finished engineering sample validation of a sixth-generation

00:01:41.457 --> 00:01:47.297
DRAM platform, built on a 4F2 cell, and it claimed to be first to complete that step.

00:01:47.297 --> 00:01:53.297
Nikkei Asia reported Samsung and SK high-nix have agreed in a patent cross-license to take

00:01:53.297 --> 00:01:57.697
some of Yangtze memory technologies' ex-tacking stacking method for 3D-NAND.

00:01:58.237 --> 00:02:03.257
A memory industry official told Fenn News the point is mostly to avoid suits after YMTC

00:02:03.257 --> 00:02:09.337
filed widely, and that YMTC's method has also left it less exposed to US equipment controls,

00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:12.457
with some leading firms now licensing the same approach.

00:02:12.457 --> 00:02:18.887
Y-Mob Group, the Hong Kong listed software firm, said on the 26th that its unit Y-Mob

00:02:18.887 --> 00:02:25.827
Giswan has signed two separate buys for 5,000 NVIDIA RTX Pro 5,500 Blackwell GPUs.

00:02:26.287 --> 00:02:32.447
Biggo Finance puts the total near 430 million yuan, about 64.6 million dollars.

00:02:33.087 --> 00:02:40.727
Ingram Micro is the larger slice, 4,000 cards for about 344 million yuan, roughly 51.7 million

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:41.147
dollars.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:47.687
Shanghai Fuxian supplies the other 1000 for $86.5 million yuan, about $13 million.

00:02:48.387 --> 00:02:53.367
The two contracts do not depend on each other, and both sellers are independent third parties.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:58.487
The cards are meant first for Y-Mob's own image, video and multimodal work.

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:04.967
Idol capacity can then be leased out. Y-Mob said it split the order because GPU supply is tight.

00:03:04.967 --> 00:03:08.698
S.K. Heinex is hunting a different kind of capacity.

00:03:09.298 --> 00:03:15.338
Digitime says it wants engineers who have worked on TSMC's 3nm process for customized

00:03:15.338 --> 00:03:20.318
high-band with memory, while Micron is adding recruiters weight in South Korea for its

00:03:20.318 --> 00:03:21.178
Asian build-out.

00:03:21.758 --> 00:03:25.838
GeForce is the release valve in a pair of trade reports tech power-up collected.

00:03:26.458 --> 00:03:32.478
Board channel says ad-in card partners have been told to expect 20-30% fewer gaming GPUs

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:36.638
from November, 2026, through January, 2027.

00:03:37.278 --> 00:03:38.618
And that note is about China.

00:03:39.238 --> 00:03:41.838
Commercial Times quoting Taiwanese ODMs

00:03:41.838 --> 00:03:45.338
puts new B-300 orders at 26 to 40 weeks

00:03:45.338 --> 00:03:50.198
and G-B-300 at about 14 to 26, with RTX Pro cards

00:03:50.198 --> 00:03:52.478
and DGX station running longer still.

00:03:53.118 --> 00:03:56.298
Industry sources expect the wafers that drop off G-Force

00:03:56.298 --> 00:03:57.898
to move toward data center chips.

00:03:58.558 --> 00:04:01.178
And Vidya has not issued that as its own shipment notice.

00:04:01.798 --> 00:04:04.818
Infinion has put a number on the box that feeds the server.

00:04:05.558 --> 00:04:11.838
EE Times describes a 5.6 kilowatt MCRPS reference design for the next common redundant power

00:04:11.838 --> 00:04:13.558
supplies and enterprise machines.

00:04:14.078 --> 00:04:17.798
That is a supply design, not a site, and not a megawatt interconnect.

00:04:18.879 --> 00:04:21.639
Yesterday's pressure from Congress was about tighter rules.

00:04:22.239 --> 00:04:23.619
Today the shipments have stopped.

00:04:24.159 --> 00:04:29.679
National Technology News, drawing on the financial times, says Nvidia told Dell and Supermicro

00:04:29.679 --> 00:04:33.499
not-to-ship servers to Malaysia, Singapore, Thailand, and Indonesia.

00:04:34.179 --> 00:04:38.239
Three people familiar with the matter are the source, and nobody has said whether the

00:04:38.239 --> 00:04:39.219
stop is temporary.

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:44.439
Cloud providers have 90 days to get licenses by showing restricted entities are not the

00:04:44.439 --> 00:04:45.139
end-users.

00:04:45.659 --> 00:04:53.119
Through its Singapore subsidiary, Nvidia booked $104 billion of revenue in 2025, 72% above

00:04:53.119 --> 00:04:53.879
the year before.

00:04:53.879 --> 00:04:56.759
On one project, the credit has already frozen.

00:04:57.439 --> 00:05:02.499
Lenders halted about $500 million for Aalani's planned computing deal with bite-dance.

00:05:03.159 --> 00:05:09.659
S&amp;P has Nvidia's AA rating on Downgrade Watch and said a one-notch cut could come within 90 days.

00:05:10.219 --> 00:05:12.919
Moody's left AA one in place, Outlook Stable.

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:18.159
The Straits Times matches the financial times on the four countries and the two server-makers.

00:05:18.159 --> 00:05:23.928
Huang and Nvidia General Counsel Tim Tetter are booked next week in front of three House

00:05:23.928 --> 00:05:27.968
Committees and the Senate Banking Committee, Domino Theory Reports.

00:05:28.608 --> 00:05:33.248
Senator Chuck Schumer wrote that Huang shipped extremely advanced chips to China in violation

00:05:33.248 --> 00:05:34.288
of export law.

00:05:34.728 --> 00:05:37.348
That is Schumer's charge, not a finding in the piece.

00:05:37.948 --> 00:05:42.688
Representative Hakim Jeffries wants export control language in next year's defense bill.

00:05:43.168 --> 00:05:47.508
Senator Elizabeth Warren said the return makes those bipartisan bills more urgent.

00:05:47.508 --> 00:05:52.748
Three Republicans on the House Foreign Affairs Committee said a short-board inquiry and

00:05:52.748 --> 00:05:55.388
a reinstatement do not clear the security questions.

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:59.408
President Trump said he personally talked the board into bringing Huang back.

00:06:00.128 --> 00:06:04.468
Bill Bishop wrote that Trump may ignore new statutes the way he set aside the Tiktok

00:06:04.468 --> 00:06:04.788
law.

00:06:05.408 --> 00:06:10.008
Chris McGuire said the bills now drafted still do not force a denial for named countries

00:06:10.008 --> 00:06:11.008
or named cases.

00:06:11.728 --> 00:06:16.888
Derek Scissors said a veto-proof statute is easier in next year's Democratic Congress, and

00:06:16.888 --> 00:06:20.988
and that the real question is whether that Congress treats export controls as a priority.

00:06:21.608 --> 00:06:26.748
The Semiconductor Industry Association has welcomed a bipartisan bill to extend the Semiconductor

00:06:26.748 --> 00:06:27.928
Investment Tax Credit.

00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:33.308
Semiconductor Digest notes the credit is set to expire at the end of 2026.

00:06:34.409 --> 00:06:38.209
A supply commitment is a promise to take capacity that is still on a calendar.

00:06:38.909 --> 00:06:45.209
Longbridge, working from NVIDIA's CFO commentary, puts supply and capacity commitments at $390

00:06:45.209 --> 00:06:45.629
billion.

00:06:45.629 --> 00:06:53.089
dollars. About 203 billion of that sits in fiscal 2028. Roughly February 2027 through

00:06:53.089 --> 00:07:01.649
January 2028. And about 92 billion in fiscal 2029. Add those two and you get 295 billion.

00:07:02.209 --> 00:07:07.309
About three quarters of the book. Park two fiscal years out. The near recorder is there,

00:07:07.629 --> 00:07:12.609
but the commentary does not break it into quarters. So it stays a remainder. Inventory

00:07:12.609 --> 00:07:14.529
is up to $39.7 billion.

00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:21.949
SK Heinex said in October, 2026, that DRAM and high bandwidth memory through 2029 is

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:26.049
largely booked once you count signed agreements and demand still being negotiated.

00:07:26.669 --> 00:07:30.349
And Nvidia's commitments grew mainly by buying that memory across years.

00:07:31.009 --> 00:07:32.189
The other stack is credit.

00:07:32.809 --> 00:07:37.649
Guarantees tied to customers and partners' land, power, buildings, and systems carry

00:07:37.649 --> 00:07:40.809
a maximum gross exposure of $118 billion.

00:07:40.809 --> 00:07:46.489
dollars. That figure is a ceiling, not a prediction of what gets drawn, and it is not a purchase

00:07:46.489 --> 00:07:51.949
order for memory. Neocloud deals still have financing, deployment, and acceptance conditions,

00:07:52.449 --> 00:07:56.849
so a customer who cannot take the machines does not turn a guarantee into a running hall.

00:07:57.529 --> 00:08:02.129
The International Energy Agency Outlook Longbridge sites puts data center electricity

00:08:02.129 --> 00:08:09.949
near 945 terawatt hours by 2030, and says about 20% of planned projects could slip on grid constraints.

00:08:09.949 --> 00:08:14.949
That 20% is a share of projects, not a slice of the 118 billion.

00:08:15.609 --> 00:08:17.949
Set them side by side, and the picture is simpler.

00:08:18.569 --> 00:08:22.549
Chip orders can be fully placed while a fifth of the buildings those chips were meant for

00:08:22.549 --> 00:08:23.989
are still waiting on a connection.

00:08:24.749 --> 00:08:29.629
The latest truce extension ran only two months, and the export rules carry a 60-day comment

00:08:29.629 --> 00:08:30.089
period.

00:08:30.569 --> 00:08:35.529
A prepayment to a supplier, which management told Tom's hardware it may offer, moves

00:08:35.529 --> 00:08:40.969
a Q, it does not issue a license and it does not close a substation. The building guarantee

00:08:40.969 --> 00:08:45.069
stops being the right instrument when the failure is no longer the customer's ability

00:08:45.069 --> 00:08:50.169
to finance a shell, but who may legally use the compute or whether the interconnect shows

00:08:50.169 --> 00:08:55.832
up before the acceptance window closes. On the horizon, the U.S.-China truce Longbridge

00:08:55.832 --> 00:09:02.512
sites expires on 10 January 2027. The Bureau of Industry and Security rule on remote access

00:09:02.512 --> 00:09:07.632
to advance semi-conductors in the Federal Register on the 19th of November, 2026,

00:09:08.272 --> 00:09:11.792
stays open for comment until the 19th of January, 2027.

00:09:12.432 --> 00:09:17.472
Huawei and CXMT are on the ISSCC draft for San Francisco next February,

00:09:17.932 --> 00:09:23.592
and the semi-conductor investment credit SIA wants extended runs out at the end of 2026.

00:09:24.332 --> 00:09:26.492
That's AI Chips and Data Centers for today.

00:09:27.072 --> 00:09:30.152
I'm Patrick and Vancouver. Thanks for listening. See you tomorrow.

